// coverage.vlt: verilator coverage config for tb/attention_top.
//
// Excludes the generated exp_lut.svh ROM (rtl/exp_lut.svh, docs/uarch.md
// 8.2/3.5) from THIS testbench's line-coverage instrumentation.
//
// Rationale: the ROM's 1024 case arms are already exhaustively covered and
// equivalence-proven, entry for entry, in tb/online_softmax
// (rom_full_sweep sweeps every one of the 1024 indices against
// model/exp_lut.hex, plus the sha256-pinned/entry-for-entry check at TB
// import time). End-to-end attention stimulus through this integration
// testbench drives 4 online_softmax lane instances at once and cannot, and
// should not try to, re-sweep all 1024 ROM arms through 4 lanes just to
// keep a generic line-coverage percentage happy: doing so would burn
// thousands of extra cycles of stimulus whose only purpose is to re-prove
// a fact already proven standalone elsewhere, and leaving the ROM
// instrumented here would poison THIS module's own coverage gate with
// 1024+ points that are not attention_top's verification target (its
// target is the FSM/round-robin-drain/NUM-accumulator/divider-bank
// integration, not the ROM contents). Verified empirically before landing
// this file: an instrumented build of online_softmax.sv alone shows 1026
// coverage points inside exp_lut.svh (out of 1045 total) with no filter,
// and exactly 0 with this `coverage_off` directive in place (total drops
// to 19), confirming the directive does what it claims for verilator
// 5.051's --coverage-line and is not a no-op.
`verilator_config
coverage_off -file "*/exp_lut.svh"
